<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria sells 3-mth 12 pct fixed coupon T-bills.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria sells 3-mth 12 pct fixed coupon T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry sold 19.863 billion levs of three-month T-bills with a fixed coupon of 12 percent, yielding 18.02 percent until maturity, central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no par value or minimum acceptable price set in advance for today's auction and was sold at an average accepted price of 94.87 percent of par.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow:</p>
<p>@</p>
<p> Issue number	     BG3031097010</p>
<p> Term			 three months</p>
<p> Auction date	     April 25</p>
<p> Issue date		 May 2</p>
<p> Maturity date	    August 1</p>
<p> Bids received	    20,023 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	94.80</p>
<p> Bids approved	    19,863 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price     94.87</p>
<p>Avg yield to maturity  18.02 pct @</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 91188</p>
